          "definition": {
            "literalString": "Virtual DOM is a structure that uses JavaScript objects to describe the real DOM tree. Whenever data updates, React first generates a new Virtual DOM tree, calculates the differences between the two trees using a Diff algorithm, and then updates only the changed parts to the real DOM."
